pageType: content
notes: |
  Technology readiness matrix slide. Presents an independent, rigorous TRL evaluation across seven core fusion subsystems and three primary confinement architectures. Clearly highlights that while scientific confinement physics has reached TRL 5 to 6, the nuclear engineering subsystems—specifically closed-loop tritium breeding and 14 MeV neutron-resistant first-wall materials—remain at TRL 3 to 4, representing the true critical path to commercialization.
elements:
  # Header Kicker
  - elementId: kicker
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 26, 600, 16]
    content:
      style: "$kicker"
      text: "03 · READINESS ASSESSMENT"

  # Header Title
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 42, 860, 30]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      text: "Scientific Feasibility (TRL 5–6) Outpaces Nuclear Engineering Readiness (TRL 3–4)"

  # Header Subtitle
  - elementId: subtitle
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 72, 860, 16]
    content:
      style: "$subtitle"
      text: "Independent TRL-style evaluation across seven critical subsystems and primary confinement architectures (Assessment as of Q3 2026)"

  # Header Divider
  - elementId: header-line
    elementType: line
    bounds: [50, 92, 860, 1]
    points: "0,0 860,0"
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

